HST Office: gtk3 clipboard queries off the main thread are made on the main thread.

An office driven over UNO hung for good (Linux, gtk3) while a mode switch or a document load ran on the UNO
request thread and built a Paste control (menubar, toolbar or ribbon): its first state asks the system
clipboard (SwBaseShell::StateClpbrd -> TransferableDataHelper::CreateFromSystemClipboard ->
GtkClipboardTransferable::getTransferDataFlavorsAsVector -> gtk_clipboard_wait_for_targets ->
g_main_loop_run). That nested loop runs the default glib main context on the request thread; the main thread
then waits for the context in g_main_context_iteration (g_cond_wait), the selection reply is never
dispatched and neither thread moves again. gdb stacks of 4 hangs of tests/runtime/check-ui-mode-cycle-stress.py
(after 0 to 19 rounds) all show this. A user's clicks run on the main thread and never met it.

The Paste state needs the targets only. Off the main thread, getTransferDataFlavorsAsVector now returns the
targets the main thread last read (HstClipboardTargets), kept fresh without waiting: an idle of the default
main context (run by the main thread only) calls gtk_clipboard_request_targets when the clipboard object is
made and at every owner change. The caller neither runs a nested loop nor releases the SolarMutex, so a Paste
state asked in the middle of a close or load over UNO cannot let the main thread run events for a frame that is
half built or half disposed. Only reading the data itself (a paste over UNO) goes to the main thread with
vcl::solarthread::syncExecute, which releases the SolarMutex while it waits; gtk_clipboard_wait_* only ever
runs on the main thread.

